# Contributing to <project> — the working protocol

> Drop this in your repo (adapted) when a second developer joins. It instantiates the
> [Cadmo collaboration protocol](https://github.com/tiagotorres91/cadmo/blob/main/docs/collaboration-protocol.md)
> — the full rationale and scars live there; this file is the operational instance.

## Roles

- **Maintainer** (<@handle>): owns `main`, production, and content verification. Reviews everything, merges everything.
- **Collaborator** (<@handle>): picks up issues, builds on branches from up-to-date `main`, opens PRs — **and stops**. Never merges, never deploys.

## The rules

1. **One demand = one issue.** All conversation happens in the issue; the PR carries code + `Closes #N`, nothing else.
2. **The spec is in the issue body** (goal, acceptance criteria, size guidance). Read the WHOLE issue including comments before starting.
3. **Every maintainer review ends with a verdict:** ✅ APPROVED (merged, done) · 🔧 CHANGES (apply and resubmit) · ❓ DECIDE (answer and wait). A closed issue may instead carry **"🤖 Resolved by maintainer"** — not your work; just absorb the change.
4. **Merge is the full stop.** New topic → new issue. Two rounds on the same point → it escalates to the humans.
5. **Every branch starts from up-to-date `main`.** Never chain PRs.

## Rule zero — run this at the START of every session

Sweep two lists (repository state is the marker, never memory):

- **A — the ball is with you:** open issues with no comments, or where the maintainer commented last.
- **B — outcomes to absorb:** closed issues without the `absorbed` label. Read the final verdict (the maintainer may have adjusted things in the merge), then add the label yourself:
  `gh issue edit <N> --add-label absorbed`

```bash
# List A
gh issue list --repo <owner>/<repo> --state open --json number,title,comments \
  --jq '.[] | select((.comments|length)==0 or .comments[-1].author.login=="<maintainer>") | "#\(.number) \(.title)"'
# List B
gh issue list --repo <owner>/<repo> --state closed --search '-label:absorbed' \
  --json number,title --jq '.[] | "#\(.number) \(.title)"'
```

## Building

Follow the project's `AGENTS.md` (the map + the definition of done). Highlights that bear repeating: acceptance criteria before code · test the real flow · say explicitly what you didn't test · production is never yours to touch.
